------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <StaggerItem> is a PURE presentational MOTION WRAPPER. Its inputs are `children` + one
display-boundary hook (useMotionPreference(350)); it renders a motion.div with `hidden`/`show` variants
that lift + fade the content in. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO
loading / error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from; the
hosted content owns its own data states). Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the
source does not have, so this surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition
the sibling presentational primitives Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095), InlineCallout (0124), and
ActiveFilterChips (0147) used. The REAL branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • full-motion entrance : hidden {opacity 0, y 15} -> shown {opacity 1, y 0} over 350 ms (web duration).
  • reduced-motion       : hidden == final state {opacity 1, y 0}, no movement (web `reduce ? {1,0}`),
                           entrance animation nil.
  • cascade delay        : index * 0.06 s (web StaggerContainer staggerChildren), suppressed when reduced.
  • empty-content leaf   : the native never-a-blank-box peer of the wrapper hosting no children.
Data source  : useMotionPreference -> StaggerItemMotionPreference.resolve (1:1 port; the live reduce flag
               binds via \.accessibilityReduceMotion, the native peer of useReducedMotion()).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : none in source (anonymous); only native a11y additions, resolved through the P1/S10 facade.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "StaggerItem" (P1/S11).
a11y         : reduce-motion honored (the core behaviour, tested); Dynamic Type via tokens; the wrapper is
               VoiceOver-transparent (adds no traits, leaving content semantics intact); the empty leaf is
               a single combined, labelled element. No interactive elements (vacuous for "label on every
               interactive element").

